<title>JAPAN: Key three-month CDs rate rises to 0.52 percent.</title>
<headline>Key three-month CDs rate rises to 0.52 percent.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's key three-month certificates of deposit (CDs) rate rose to 0.52 percent on Wednesday, the highest level since November 13, traders said.  </p>
<p>About 270 billion yen worth of new three-month CDs were issued, a city bank trader said.</p>
<p>The rise in the CD rate was due to increased fund demand toward the year-end, the trader said.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-5473-3748</p>
